# `actuarial::life_contingencies::curtate_curve`

Expected remaining complete years at every duration.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series actuarial::life_contingencies::curtate_curve(const pluss::Series &qx);
```

## What It Does

Entry `t` is the expected number of complete years lived after duration `t`, within the horizon, for `t = 0, 1, …, n`: {math}`e_t=\sum_{k>t}{}_{k-t}p_{x+t}`. The curve has `n + 1` entries; the first equals [`curtate_mean`](curtate_mean.md) and the last, at the end of the horizon, is 0. It falls as the remaining horizon shrinks.

## Parameters

`qx`
: One-dimensional series of probabilities in {math}`[0,1]`.

## Returns

A series of `qx.numel() + 1` values, ending at 0.

## Errors

Throws the `survival_curve: …` errors of invalid probabilities.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: the curve

Three years of mortality.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  out.writeln(life::curtate_curve(pluss::make_series({0.1, 0.2, 0.3})).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2: the start and end

The first value is the mean and the last is zero.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  const auto c = life::curtate_curve(qx).items<double>();
  out.writeln("first =", c.front(), " curtate_mean =", life::curtate_mean(qx).item<double>(), " last =", c.back());
}
```

### Example 3: the recursion by hand

{math}`e_t=p_t\,(1+e_{t+1})`, working back from the end.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto c = life::curtate_curve(pluss::make_series({0.1, 0.2, 0.3})).items<double>();
  out.writeln(0.9 * (1.0 + c[1]), c[0]);
  out.writeln(0.8 * (1.0 + c[2]), c[1]);
  out.writeln(0.7 * (1.0 + c[3]), c[2]);
}
```

### Example 4: no mortality

Every remaining year is lived, so the curve counts down.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  out.writeln(life::curtate_curve(pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.0, 0.0})).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 5: the error

An invalid probability.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)life::curtate_curve(pluss::make_series({0.1, -0.2})); });
}
```

